The commercial space industry is growing rapidly, with companies working to make space exploration and travel more affordable and accessible.
Several companies are contributing to this development, including:
Company	Main Activities
Virgin Galactic	Provides suborbital spaceflights.
Rocket Lab	Provides launch services for small satellites.
Blue Origin	Manufactures reusable rockets for suborbital and orbital spaceflight.
SpaceX	Develops and operates reusable rockets, spacecraft, and satellite internet services.
Among these companies, SpaceX has achieved significant success in commercial spaceflight.
